# Design System — Figma Sync Rules

## Figma MCP Workflow (required for component changes)

When implementing or updating a component from Figma, follow this order:

1. Read `figma/component-manifest.json` for the component's `figmaNodeId`, `codePath`, and prop mappings
2. Run `get_design_context(fileKey, nodeId)` to fetch structured layout, props, and tokens
3. Run `get_screenshot(fileKey, nodeId)` for visual reference
4. Only then edit the React component, story, and Code Connect template
5. Use design token CSS variables (`var(--color-bg-primary)`) — never hardcode hex colors or pixel values
6. Use Tailwind classes that reference token variables (e.g. `bg-color-bg-primary`, `p-spacing-md`)
7. Validate the implementation against the Figma screenshot before marking complete
8. Update `figma/component-manifest.json` if props or variants changed

## Token Rules

- Token source files live in `packages/tokens/src/*.json` (W3C Design Tokens format)
- Generated files in `packages/tokens/dist/` are AUTO-GENERATED — never edit manually
- Run `pnpm build:tokens` after token changes
- Figma Variable Code Syntax must match: `color/bg/primary` → `var(--color-bg-primary)`

## Component Conventions

- One folder per component: `packages/ui/src/{Component}/`
- Files: `{Component}.tsx`, `{Component}.stories.tsx`, `{Component}.figma.ts`
- Export from `packages/ui/src/index.ts`
- Props must match `figma/component-manifest.json` definitions
- Co-locate Storybook stories with components; Storybook picks them up automatically

## Code Connect

- Template files use `figma.selectedInstance` with prop mappings from manifest
- Publish with `npx figma connect publish --token=$FIGMA_TOKEN`
- Each template `id` must match `codeConnectId` in the manifest

## Sync Commands

```bash
pnpm sync:figma      # Pull Figma Variables → packages/tokens/src/
pnpm push:figma      # Push local tokens → Figma (bidirectional)
pnpm sync:manifest   # Validate manifest against code files
pnpm build:tokens    # Rebuild CSS, Tailwind theme, TS tokens
pnpm storybook       # Local Storybook at http://localhost:6006
```

## Automated Sync (CI)

- Token changes: `.github/workflows/sync-tokens.yml` (cron + webhook)
- Component changes: `.github/workflows/sync-components.yml` (LIBRARY_PUBLISH webhook)
- On Figma library publish, agent reads manifest → fetches design context → updates code → opens PR

## Do Not

- Hardcode colors, spacing, or font sizes in components
- Edit generated token output files
- Skip the Figma screenshot validation step
- Create components without updating the manifest
